    config IR_AC_MODEL
        int "Air conditioner model"
        default 1
        range -1 32767
        help
            Model of the remote for protocols with several variants (IRremoteESP8266 *_ac_remote_model_t),
            -1 or 1 for the default one. Used until a model is selected with a double click on BOOT
            (that one is kept in NVS, a factory reset goes back to this value). FUJITSU_AC: 1 ARRAH2E, 2 ARDB1, 3 ARREB1E, 4 ARJW2, 5 ARRY4,
            6 ARREW4E. See SupportedProtocols.md of IRremoteESP8266 for the other protocols.

    config IR_AC_HALF_DEGREES
        bool "Send half degrees"
        default n
        help
            The setpoint is sent in 0.5 degC steps. Most remotes only send whole degrees (e.g. Fujitsu ARRAH2E,
            ARDB1, ARREB1E: a half degree makes the message invalid for the unit), so by default the setpoint is
            rounded to a whole degree. Enable it only for remotes with half degrees (e.g. Fujitsu ARREW4E).

    config IR_AC_MODEL_MAX
        int "Number of models (double click on BOOT)"
        default 6 if IR_AC_PROTOCOL_FUJITSU_AC
        default 1
        range 1 32
        help
            A double click on the BOOT button selects the next model (1 .. this value, then 1 again), keeps it in
            NVS and sends the state with it. To find the model of the remote without rebuilding.
            FUJITSU_AC has 6 models.

    config IR_TX_GPIO
        int "IR transmitter GPIO"
        default 4
        range 0 ENV_GPIO_OUT_RANGE_MAX
        help
            GPIO driving the IR LED (through a transistor). Do not use the button or the status LED GPIO.

    config IR_RX_GPIO
        int "IR receiver GPIO"
        default 5
        range -1 ENV_GPIO_OUT_RANGE_MAX
        help
            Output of the IR receiver module (TSOP38238, VS1838B, ... at 38 kHz). Received messages are decoded and
            logged ("[IR RX]"). -1: no receiver.

    config IR_RX_DECODE_ALL
        bool "Decode all protocols (needs much more flash)"
        default n
        help
            The receiver decodes the selected air conditioner protocol and NEC. With this option every decoder of
            IRremoteESP8266 is compiled, to find the protocol of an unknown remote. It may not fit into the OTA
            partition next to Matter, disable it again when the protocol is known.

    config IR_TX_INVERTED
        bool "Inverted IR output"
        default n
        help
            The IR LED is on when the GPIO is LOW. Only for driver circuits which need it.

endmenu
